//! Zamani Quantum Benchmarking — Canonical Report Model
//!
//! Production-grade reporting boundary for all Zamani quantum benchmarks.
//!
//! # Architectural role
//!
//! This module owns the canonical, format-independent representation of a
//! benchmark report.
//!
//! It deliberately does NOT:
//!
//! - execute quantum circuits;
//! - generate workloads;
//! - calculate benchmark metrics;
//! - perform statistical fitting;
//! - compare hardware;
//! - perform regression analysis;
//! - mutate benchmark results;
//! - select a backend;
//! - depend on a hardware provider;
//! - depend on a simulator;
//! - depend on a concrete benchmark protocol.
//!
//! Its responsibility is:
//!
//! ```text
//! BenchmarkResult
//!       │
//!       ▼
//! reporting::report
//!       │
//!       ├────────► canonical report model
//!       │
//!       ├────────► deterministic JSON representation
//!       │
//!       ├────────► human-readable text
//!       │
//!       └────────► downstream Markdown / CSV / table renderers
//! ```
//!
//! # Why this is a separate model
//!
//! `BenchmarkResult` is the scientific/result interchange contract.
//!
//! `BenchmarkReport` is the presentation contract.
//!
//! Keeping these separate is essential:
//!
//! ```text
//! protocol
//!    │
//!    ▼
//! BenchmarkResult
//!    │
//!    ├──► analysis
//!    ├──► registry
//!    ├──► CI
//!    ├──► persistence
//!    │
//!    └──► BenchmarkReport
//!              │
//!              ├── JSON
//!              ├── Markdown
//!              ├── text
//!              ├── table
//!              └── future formats
//! ```
//!
//! A report therefore never becomes the authoritative scientific data model.
//!
//! # Production properties
//!
//! This implementation provides:
//!
//! - deterministic report construction;
//! - bounded report size;
//! - bounded title/description/section sizes;
//! - deterministic section ordering;
//! - deterministic key ordering through `BTreeMap`;
//! - JSON-safe output;
//! - no floating-point formatting surprises in the canonical JSON payload;
//! - explicit report schema version;
//! - explicit source-result identity;
//! - explicit generation metadata;
//! - structured sections;
//! - structured findings;
//! - structured warnings;
//! - structured errors;
//! - stable machine-readable field names;
//! - human-readable rendering;
//! - JSON rendering;
//! - report validation;
//! - protection against pathological serialized results;
//! - no process-global state;
//! - no timestamps generated implicitly;
//! - no hostname/environment leakage;
//! - no logging/printing from the library;
//! - Rust 1.97 / 1.97.1 compatibility;
//! - Rust 2021 compatibility;
//! - no unsafe code.
//!
//! # Important privacy/reproducibility rule
//!
//! This module never automatically adds:
//!
//! - hostname;
//! - username;
//! - IP address;
//! - filesystem paths;
//! - environment variables;
//! - process ID;
//! - machine serial numbers;
//! - cloud credentials;
//! - access tokens;
//! - API keys;
//! - arbitrary environment metadata.
//!
//! Such information must already be intentionally represented by the
//! authoritative benchmark provenance layer.
//!
//! This prevents a seemingly harmless report operation from leaking local
//! environment information.
//!
//! # Determinism
//!
//! The report model is deterministic when its input `BenchmarkResult` is
//! deterministic.
//!
//! In particular:
//!
//! - sections are kept in insertion order only when explicitly supplied;
//! - arbitrary maps are normalized into sorted `BTreeMap`s;
//! - JSON object serialization is based on `BTreeMap` ordering;
//! - no current time is inserted automatically;
//! - no random identifier is generated.
//!
//! # Integration contract
//!
//! This module consumes:
//!
//! ```text
//! quantum::benchmarking::core::Result::BenchmarkResult
//! ```
//!
//! The current repository uses a capitalized `Result.rs` filename. This module
//! therefore intentionally imports `super::super::core::Result` rather than
//! assuming a lowercase `result.rs` that does not currently exist.
//!
//! Future modules integrate downstream:
//!
//! ```text
//! core::Result
//!       │
//!       ▼
//! reporting::report
//!       │
//!       ├── reporting::summary
//!       ├── reporting::table
//!       ├── reporting::json
//!       ├── reporting::csv
//!       └── reporting::markdown
//! ```
//!
//! None of those future modules need to change this report model merely
//! because they are introduced.
//!
//! # Rust compatibility
//!
//! Target:
//!
//! - Rust 1.97
//! - Rust 1.97.1
//! - Rust 2021
//!
//! No nightly features.
//! No unsafe code.
//!
//! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#![deny(unsafe_code)]
#![deny(unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn)]
#![deny(unused_must_use)]

